# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download Python and use a virtual environment with Qiskit (recommended).\n"
msgstr "Unduh Python dan gunakan virtual environment dengan Qiskit (direkomendasikan).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Click to expand for more information about **Python**.\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Klik untuk melihat informasi lebih lanjut tentang **Python**.\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To install Python, first check the \"Programming Language\" section on the [Qiskit PyPI project page](https://pypi.org/project/qiskit/) to determine which Python versions are supported by the most recent release. For download instructions, see the [Python Beginners Guide](https://wiki.python.org/moin/BeginnersGuide/Download).\n"
msgstr "Untuk menginstal Python, cek dulu bagian \"Programming Language\" di [halaman proyek Qiskit di PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/qiskit/) untuk mengetahui versi Python mana yang didukung oleh rilis terbaru. Untuk instruksi unduhan, lihat [Panduan Python untuk Pemula.](https://wiki.python.org/moin/BeginnersGuide/Download)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: </AccordionItem>
# <AccordionItem title="Klik untuk melihat in
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"These instructions use the standard Python distribution from [pypi.org](https://pypi.org/). However, you can use other Python distributions, such as [Anaconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/anaconda/) or [miniconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/), along with other dependency management workflows like [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/docs/).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"Click to expand for more information on **virtual environments**.\">\n"
"    - Use [Python virtual environments](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html) to separate Qiskit from other applications.\n"
"    A Python virtual environment is an isolated space to work with Python for a specific purpose — so you can install whatever packages you wish, and set up libraries, dependencies, and so on, without affecting the \"base\" Python environment on your machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"Klik untuk memperluas informasi lebih lanjut tentang **virtual environment**.\">\n"
"    - Gunakan [virtual environment Python](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html) untuk memisahkan Qiskit dari aplikasi lain.\n"
"    Virtual environment Python adalah ruang terisolasi untuk bekerja dengan Python untuk tujuan tertentu — jadi kamu bisa menginstal paket apa pun yang kamu inginkan, dan menyiapkan library, dependency, dan sebagainya, tanpa memengaruhi environment Python \"base\" di komputermu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    One important advantage of a virtual environment is that if your Python environment becomes corrupted, you can easily delete it and start over!\n"
msgstr "    Salah satu keunggulan penting dari virtual environment adalah jika lingkungan Python-mu rusak, Anda bisa dengan mudah menghapusnya dan mulai dari awal!\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Choose a preferred location in which to store information about your virtual environments. Typically they're stored in a directory named `.venv` within each project directory.\n"
msgstr "    Pilih lokasi yang Anda suka untuk menyimpan informasi tentang virtual environment-mu. Biasanya disimpan di direktori bernama `.venv` di dalam setiap direktori proyek.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    To set up a virtual environment, navigate to your project directory and create a minimal environment with only Python installed in it.\n"
msgstr "    Untuk membuat virtual environment, navigasi ke direktori proyekmu dan buat lingkungan minimal yang hanya berisi Python.\n"

